 according to his high school.","published":"2026-11-14T20:36:58.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482223/georgia-football-commit-marcellus-young-casario-dies-suddenly","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Oklahoma AD 'infuriated' with SEC, Ole Miss for Sunday game","description":"AD Roger Denny took aim at the SEC and Ole Miss about Oklahoma's game being moved to Sunday, calling it an \"inexplicable\" situation that \"unfairly burdens\" the Sooners.","published":"2026-11-14T20:28:29.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482206/oklahoma-ad-infuriated-sec-ole-miss-sunday-game","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Clemson QB Tait Reynolds suffers leg injury on slide","description":"Clemson quarterback Tait Reynolds was knocked out of the Tigers' game against Georgia Tech on Saturday after injuring his knee on a run play.","published":"2026-11-14T20:47:42.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482105/clemson-qb-tait-reynolds-suffers-leg-injury-slide","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Central Oklahoma AD trolls Ole Miss amid FAA crisis-forced kickoff change","description":"The Division II school offered Ole Miss fans attending its Oklahoma matchup free admission due to the kickoff date change.","published":"2026-11-14T20:09:11.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481529/central-oklahoma-troll-ole-miss-faa-decsion","type":"Story","byline":"Kalan Hooks","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Watch best moments and top plays live from Week 11","published":"2026-11-14T18:48:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50474063/week-11-live-highlights","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Ohio State's Jeremiah Smith sets Big Ten receiving record","description":"Ohio State wide receiver Jeremiah Smith broke yet another record, eclipsing the Big Ten mark for career receiving yards during the first half vs. Northwestern.","published":"2026-11-14T20:31:59.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481134/ohio-state-jeremiah-smith-sets-big-ten-receiving-record","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Tracking Ohio State WR Jeremiah Smith's record-setting 2026 season","description":"Ohio State's superstar receiver has made breaking records a weekly occurrence this fall.","published":"2026-11-14T18:05:18.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50142903/jeremiah-smith-ohio-state-record-tracker","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Alabama makes last-second call to start QB Keelon Russell","description":"No. 3 Alabama made a last-second decision to start Keelon Russell against Vanderbilt after the quarterback looked better than anticipated in pregame warmups.","published":"2026-11-14T18:56:15.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50480988/alabama-makes-last-second-call-start-qb-keelon-russell","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Maryland QB Malik Washington doesn't start vs. Wisconsin","description":"Maryland quarterback Malik Washington did not start against Wisconsin as he continues to deal with a lower-body injury.","published":"2026-11-14T17:50:19.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50480722/source-maryland-qb-malik-washington-start-vs-wisconsin","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Colorado upsets No. 14 Houston for first AP top-15 win since 2007","description":"Colorado posted its first victory over an AP top-15 team since 2007 in beating No. 14 Houston 42-32 and slightly cooled down the hot seat for coach Deion Sanders.","published":"2026-11-14T14:22:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50479172/colorado-upsets-no-14-houston-1st-ap-top-15-win-2007","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5079678/justin-scott","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Scott_(American_football)"},"pick":{"pick":52,"round":2,"team":"NE","provisional":true},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Justin Scott (American football)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Scott_(American_football)","description":"American football player (born 2006)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:27Z","intro":"Justin Scott (born January 31, 2006) is an American college football defensive tackle for the Miami Hurricanes.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Scott is from Chicago, Illinois. He grew up playing basketball before being convinced by his coach and a friend at St. Ignatius College Prep to try out football as a freshman in high school. A defensive tackle, he played for the sophomore team in his freshman year. As a sophomore, he appeared in only one game for the varsity team, yet he began receiving many scholarship offers to play college football. He was a starter as a defensive lineman and offensive guard as a junior, posting 42 tackles, 13 tackles-for-loss (TFLs) and 4.5 sacks.\nAs a senior in 2023, Scott posted 28 tackles, seven TFLs and two sacks while earning selection to the All-American Bowl. He helped St. Ignatius to an appearance in the Class 8A quarterfinals as a senior and was named the Friday Night Drive Defensive Player of the Year as well as all-state. In addition to football, Scott also played basketball in high school. A five-star recruit, he was ranked one of the top 15 prospects nationally in the class of 2024. He initially committed to play college football for the Ohio State Buckeyes in July 2023. He later flipped his commitment to the Miami Hurricanes in November 2023."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Prior to Scott's true freshman season, he was named to Bruce Feldman of The Athletic's \"Freaks List\", highlighting the most athletic college football players. He was a backup during the 2024 season and finished with seven tackles, two tackles-for-loss and a sack while appearing in 12 games. He saw more playing time as a sophomore, starting several games while posting 19 tackles, 6.5 TFLs and a sack in the regular season."}]}}